{"type": "say", "text": "Thanks everyone for being here. As you know, the customer-notification service needs a production message-streaming platform before its next integration milestone, and we've narrowed it down to two finalists: KafkaCloud and StreamGrid. Both passed our benchmark of 20,000 messages per second with sub-250-millisecond median delivery latency. The draft architecture currently recommends StreamGrid based on simpler operational setup and an initial capacity estimate of four brokers. Before I make a final decision, I'd like to go through sign-off from each of your areas -- backend, support engineering, security, and FinOps. Could each of you share your assessment of the two platforms, starting with any concerns or considerations from your perspective?"}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "I need to flag something important before we go further. While testing the notification client's retry behavior this morning, I confirmed that the service already has a KafkaCloud-compatible producer and consumer path. This means using KafkaCloud would only require about two days of adapter cleanup, whereas moving to StreamGrid would require a new two-week client integration. I haven't updated the architecture document with this yet, but it directly affects the StreamGrid recommendation -- the simpler operational setup comes with a significantly longer integration timeline that wasn't reflected in the draft."}
```

