{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF4", "text": "I need to share something from the FinOps side that I found this morning when I reconciled the cloud account. We already have existing KafkaCloud reserved-capacity credits that cover exactly six production brokers through the service's first year. StreamGrid has no equivalent credit. This means a KafkaCloud production deployment would provision all six brokers -- setting production_broker_count to exactly 6 to use the full reserved-capacity allocation -- at no additional cost for the first year. I should note that I have not yet amended the four-broker estimate in the draft architecture, so that figure doesn't reflect this reserved-capacity allocation."}
```

